From dc4fb35aff0ceebecee769af2d88891d59915a5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Armen Zambrano G." <44410+armenzg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Jan 2026 08:32:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chore(overwatch): Remove Overwatch forwarding infrastructure
 (#106447)

This PR removes all Overwatch-related forwarding infrastructure from
Sentry, simplifying the code review webhook flow to send events directly
to Seer.

**Key Changes:**

- **Removed modules**: Deleted `src/sentry/overwatch/` and
`src/sentry/overwatch_webhooks/` directories entirely
- **Removed RPC endpoints**: Deleted 4 internal RPC endpoints
(`/internal/prevent/pr-review/*` and
`/internal/code-review/repo-settings/`)
- **Removed RPC service**: Deleted `OverwatchConsentService` and related
consent checking logic
- **Simplified webhook routing**: GitHub webhooks (`pull_request`,
`issue_comment`) now flow directly to Seer without conditional routing
- **Removed configuration**: Cleaned up Overwatch-specific settings
(`OVERWATCH_RPC_SHARED_SECRET`, `OVERWATCH_REGION_URLS`, webhook
forwarding options)
- **Updated metrics**: Changed `overwatch.code_review.*` metric to
`seer.code_review.error.*`
- **Removed organization deletion hooks**: No longer notifies Overwatch
when organizations are deleted

The webhook flow is now simpler and more direct, with no intermediate
Overwatch layer.

